Weekly TikTok autopilot for Anesthesia Study Co. LLC (ASC), owned by Andrea Regan, CAA. Goal: get the word out about ASC so anesthesia students (AA/CAA, SRNA/CRNA), trainees and early-career providers follow and come back daily. 2 faceless TikTok reels per day, every day, auto-published via Metricool:
- 12:30 PM America/New_York: company spotlight (format "brand"). This is always the first post of the day.
- 8:30 PM America/New_York: educational Quick Case (format "case").
Once TikTok has 2+ weeks of data, use getBestTimeToPostByNetwork (tiktok) and move the two slots to the best times (keep the company post first and the slots at least 5 hours apart).
Everything is faceless: animated graphics, monitors and product mockups only. No people, no faces, no AI imagery. Never name Andrea, a university, professor or exam.

Company message (source: ASC author bio; reword every time, never paste): ASC creates practical, student-centered resources for anesthesia learners, clinical trainees and early-career providers, built around the realities of anesthesia training: organization, clinical readiness, case tracking, board-style review and high-yield OR reference tools. Mission: help students bridge classroom learning and clinical practice with clear, organized, easy-to-use study and documentation resources that build confidence, consistency and professional growth. Products: clinical logbooks and case trackers, study guides, quick-reference tools, board-prep resources, mind maps, medication study cards, coloring study books, BLS/ACLS training. Promise: stay organized, track clinical progress, build confidence from classroom to OR.

0. GATE: call getBrandSettings (brand 6389044). If networksData has no TikTok account, do NOT build or post anything. Send Andrea ONE short SendUserMessage: "TikTok autopilot is ready but TikTok isn't connected in Metricool yet. Create the @anesthesiastudyco TikTok (switch it to a Business account), then in Metricool open the Anesthesia Study Co LLC brand → Connections → TikTok. The first week will queue on the next Saturday run." Then stop.

1. Clone the media branch: git clone --depth 1 --branch social-media https://github.com/anesthesiastudycollc-cyber/ASC-Website.git ~/asc-media (use add_repo with push access for anesthesiastudycollc-cyber/ASC-Website first if needed). Read _src/TIKTOK.md fully (brand kit, daily slots, weekday rotation table, spec fields, caption rules, topic log) and _src/PLAYBOOK.md (clinical accuracy rules, book map, website rules). Generator: _src/gen_tiktok.py (fonts in _src/fonts; logo used automatically if _src/brand/logo.png exists). Example spec: _src/tiktok-sample.json. If _src/gen_tiktok.py or _src/TIKTOK.md is missing, do NOT build or post anything: send Andrea one short SendUserMessage saying the TikTok generator files (gen_tiktok.py, TIKTOK.md, tiktok-sample.json) still need to be added to the _src folder of the social-media branch, then stop.

2. If TikTok has data, pull the last 7 days from Metricool for tiktok (use getAnalyticsAvailableMetrics to find views, average watch time, likes, shares, saves, comments, followers). Note which hooks, topics and formats won and lean into them.

3. getScheduledPosts for the next 9 days (tiktok). Plan 14 reels for the 7 days starting the next day that has no TikTok post yet (never two posts in the same slot):
   - Seven 12:30 PM "brand" spotlights following the TIKTOK.md weekday rotation (Meet ASC, Logbook, Mind Maps, Study Guides, Study Cards, On Amazon, BLS+ACLS/website). Each week a fresh hook, kicker, 3 points and outro: show what's inside, who it's for and how it helps on a clinical day, not just "buy". Mind maps $5 each on anesthesiastudyco.com; study guides on Etsy; books on Amazon; app "coming soon" (never a date).
   - Seven 8:30 PM "case" reels: clinically accurate per PLAYBOOK rules, vivid scene with real-looking vitals (set alarm true on abnormal values), 4 options, one correct, why ≤ 40 words, pearl ≤ 14 words. You may re-cut strong Instagram topics older than 2 weeks (new hook and scene, not a copy). Mix in series hooks that build a daily habit ("Day N of Airway Week", "Would you extubate?").
   - Check the TIKTOK.md topic log: no topic repeats within 8 weeks.
   TikTok caption rules: first line is a scroll-stopping hook (under 100 characters), 1-3 short lines, CTA (comment your pick / save / follow @anesthesiastudyco), then "📚 More: Anesthesia Study Co. on Amazon + anesthesiastudyco.com (link in bio)", then 4-6 hashtags (#anesthesia #anesthesiastudent #crna #srna #caa #anesthesiastudyco, swapping in topic tags). No patient identifiers.

4. Write _src/tiktokN-am.json (7 brand posts) and _src/tiktokN-pm.json (7 case posts). Run python3 -I _src/gen_tiktok.py tiktokN-am.json <work>/tiktok-am and the pm spec to <work>/tiktok-pm. Make a contact sheet of key frames from every reel (brand: ~1.5, 2.9, 7.8, 10.5, 12.2, 14.5 s; case: ~2, 4.5, 8, 10.5, 14, 20 s) and look at it yourself; fix clipped, overlapping or off-safe-zone text and re-render before publishing. Add every new topic to the TIKTOK.md topic log.

5. Copy outputs into ~/asc-media/tiktok/am/<date>/ and ~/asc-media/tiktok/pm/<date>/ (reel.mp4 + cover.jpg), add both specs and the updated _src/TIKTOK.md, commit (author "Anesthesia Study Co"; end the message with the Co-Authored-By/Claude-Session lines from your session reminder if present), pull --rebase if needed, push to social-media. Media URLs: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/anesthesiastudycollc-cyber/ASC-Website@<pushed-hash>/tiktok/<am|pm>/<date>/reel.mp4 with videoThumbnailUrl .../cover.jpg.

6. createScheduledPost for each (blogId 6389044, providers [{"network":"tiktok"}], autoPublish true, draft false, publicationDate 12:30 or 20:30 America/New_York with the correct UTC offset in date). tiktokData: privacyOption PUBLIC_TO_EVERYONE, disableComment/Duet/Stitch false, isAigc false (programmatic graphics), commercialContentOwnBrand true on the 7 brand posts and false on the 7 case posts. Never touch Instagram posts. Confirm each response shows the media copied to Metricool.

7. Finish with a short SendUserMessage to Andrea: last week's TikTok numbers (views, avg watch time, follows, shares) vs the week before, what worked, the 14 queued posts (date, slot, hook), the contact sheet via SendUserFile, and 1-2 faceless ideas she could make herself (screen recording, hands-only page flip of a book or logbook, voiceover over a product). If any step fails (GitHub push refused, Metricool error), do not post anything partial; tell her exactly what failed and what to do.
